{
  "title": "Salat of وَ وَاعَدْنَا",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "At each of these ten nights, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer between the Maghrib and Isha’ obligatory prayers and to recite at each unit Surah al-Faatehah once, Surah al-Tawheed once, and the following verse (7/142):\nوَ وَاعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلَاثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً \nWA WAA-A’DNAA MOOSAA SALAASEENA LAYLATAN\nAnd We appointed with Moses a time of thirty nights \nوَ اَتْمَمْنَاهَا بِعَشْرٍ \nWA ATMAMNAAHAA BE-A’SHRIN\nand completed them with ten more, \nفَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً\nFA-TAMMA MEEQAATO RABBEHI ARBA-E’ENA LAYLATAN\nso the appointed time of his Lord was complete forty nights, \nوَ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هَارُوْنَ\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LE-AKHEEHE HAAROONAKH\nand Moses said to his brother Aaron: \nاخْلُفْنِيْ فِيْ قَوْمِيْ وَ اَصْلِحْ\nLUFNEE FEE QAWMEE WA ASLEH\nTake my place among my people, and act well \nوَ لَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ.\nWA LAA TATTA-BE’ SABEELAL MUFSEDEEN.\nand do not follow the way of the mischief-makers.\nThe reward of offering this prayer is to participate in the rewards of those who go on Hajj."
}
